# CLI

Every binary is a Cobra CLI. `main` only executes the root command. All runtime configuration goes through Viper (flags, env, optional config file). Do not parse `os.Args`, use `flag`, or read env vars directly in command code.

```go
// ❌ BAD
func main() {
    level := os.Getenv("OBS_LOG_LEVEL")
    _ = obs.New().Run(context.Background(), &mcp.StdioTransport{})
}

// ✅ GOOD
func main() {
    if err := rootCmd.ExecuteContext(context.Background()); err != nil {
        slog.Error("command failed", "err", err)
        os.Exit(1)
    }
}

var rootCmd = &cobra.Command{
    Use: "obs",
    PersistentPreRunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {
        return initConfig()
    },
    RunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {
        return obs.New().Run(cmd.Context(), &mcp.StdioTransport{})
    },
}
```
